The branch is story-1221a-compile-refusals, checked out in this worktree at 3defb62ac. That is 7c969aa5d (0109a2's head, #1222) plus round 1's six commits. Do not rebase, squash, amend or merge anything. When you are done, the branch is 3defb62ac plus your commits.

WHAT ROUND 1 DID (run story-unit-1221a-for-issues-1221-17e595f7, IMPL-BLOCKED on item 1 only). Read its six commit messages (`git log 7c969aa5d..3defb62ac`), and do not redo them:
- 9730cce57: item 2, `BodyRefusal::UnanimousPassUnderResidual`;
- 3f95bdd4a: item 3, the body's refusal reported first;
- 9fe6f5c2d: item 4, `SequenceStep::declares_change`;
- f6c08db77: item 5, core's residual names from `ResidualInput`;
- 50791c09d: item 6, the guide's sentence;
- 3defb62ac: test builders for the clones gate.

WHY ITEM 1 BLOCKED, AND WHY THE BLOCK IS THE ENGINE'S. Round 1 found that #1212's L1 premise is wrong.
- **What it found.** The shipped recipes/gpt-flash protects `review`, through fast's `protected_phase`. Every select case there is a sequence [positions, chief]:
  - `positions` is a review-panel of WORK-class members. DSH is an untrusted work provider and cannot judge gates (recipes/gpt-flash/README.md);
  - `positions` declares `security-hold`, a hard word, so its compiled `ends_on` holds it.
  The commissioned compile refusal therefore refused a shipped recipe.
- **The engine behind it.** 0109a1's bb7a73b67 made "a lawful early ending at a work step before every gate in a protected body" refuse at decide as `Unrecorded`. Its claim that no shipped protected phase is a sequence missed gpt-flash. So today a gpt-flash panel's `security-hold` PARKS where it should STOP. That fails closed, but it breaks three accepted rules:
  - 0050 ruling 5: "`security-hold` rules a hard stop from every phase that admits it … and, under ruling 7, from every step of a sequence";
  - 0050 ruling 7: a non-final step's hard word "ends the sequence with that word wherever it is reported: a panel's `security-hold` is the machine's";
  - 0109's "What stays out": "The `security-hold` stop and the residual rules stand", and "No refusal is weakened … `security-hold` stop stand[s]".
- **The fix the controller took** (option (c) of round 1's four, as recommended under the standing ruling of 2026-11-04). It implements the accepted rules and amends none:
  - the engine takes the compiled pre-gate hard stop;
  - the compiler refuses only a pre-gate ending the engine can never take.
- **The other three options, and why each is out:**
  - (a) gate-class gpt-flash members: DSH cannot judge gates;
  - (b) `positions` dropping `security-hold`: a member's hold would then fail the step;
  - (d) an unprincipled exemption.

THE RE-SCOPED ITEM 1 (two commits, each with its tests and a removal control in its message):

**1a. decide takes a protected sequence's compiled pre-gate hard stop.**
- **The case.** The terminal stands at a work step before every gate step of a protected body. Its word is in that step's compiled `ends_on`, and is a hard word: every table arm for it is `hard` and goes to a phase that stops the run (`bundle::sequence::stops_run`, the one test `hard_results` and the engine's `request_or_finish` use).
- **The rule.** That terminal is admitted with no gate record. A stop ships no head, so there is no head to decide on. The table rules its hard arm (gpt-flash's `security-hold`: REVIEW-SECURITY-HOLD → stop), and ship is never requested.
  - Today the refusal is at crates/brokkr-runtime/src/engine/verdict.rs (`step_head`, the `(_, None, Some(first))` arm at about :386-389). It is reached through `Producer::of` with the terminal's word. Find where the word and the compiled step's `ends_on` are both in hand, and admit the case there.
  - Whatever head the decide inputs carry for a stop, say which, and show that no ship-bound arm can read it.
- **What stays refused, unchanged:**
  - a pre-gate work step's ending on a word that does NOT stop the run (`Unrecorded`, as today);
  - a terminal at a pre-gate step on a word outside its `ends_on` (`Unlawful`);
  - every other `ObservationProblem` (M1 to M5, X1).
- **This is 0109a1's reviewed code** (seven security holds). Change only this case, add no refactor beside it, and keep `Unrecorded`'s and `Unlawful`'s text.
- **Tests, through the real engine:**
  - shipped recipes/gpt-flash, compiled from recipes/ with only its drivers scripted: a `positions` member reports `security-hold` with a high security finding, so the aggregate says `security-hold`. The run rules REVIEW-SECURITY-HOLD and stops. It never parks, never runs the chief, and never requests ship;
  - the same body with the members `clean` reaches the chief and decides on the chief's gate record, as today;
  - a test-only protected [work, gate] body whose work step ends on a NON-hard word still refuses `Unrecorded` and parks;
  - a re-tag of the terminal to that work step on a word outside `ends_on` still refuses `Unlawful`;
  - 0109a1's observation tests (verdict::observation_tests, bb7a73b67's among them) pass unchanged, apart from the one test that pinned today's hard-stop park, if there is one. Name it, and say why it moved.
- **Removal control:** restore the `Unrecorded` arm for the hard case, and the gpt-flash test parks.

**1b. The compiler refuses a protected sequence's pre-gate ending on a word that does not stop the run.**
- After 1a, that ending is the one the engine can never take. It routes onward with no gate record, so decide refuses it.
- Refuse at compile a protected phase's sequence when a step before its first gate step has a compiled `ends_on` word that is NOT a hard word. Use the compiler's own protected-phase knowledge (fast's `protected_phase`), never a name (0107).
- Round 1's saved patch, .forge/item1-l1-pre-gate-hard-ending.patch (untracked, against 7c969aa5d), has the refusal, its `BodyRefusal`-style variant and three tests. Rebase it by hand onto `BodyRefusal`, which round 1 moved to bundle/aggregate.rs, and narrow it to non-hard words.
- **Tests:**
  - a protected [work, gate] body whose work step may end on a non-hard word is refused, naming the seat, step and word;
  - the same with a hard word (gpt-flash's shape) compiles;
  - an unprotected phase compiles;
  - every shipped recipe compiles, through the library walk (`bundle::sequence_tests::every_shipped_sequence_…`).
- **Removal control:** skip the check, and the first test compiles.

THE OPERATOR'S RULING: the standing ruling of 2026-11-04 ("go with recommended on anything else that comes up", "and by hand") covers this round, option (c), the narrowed L1, and any public-API line they add. It implements 0050 rulings 5 and 7 and 0109's "What stays out", and amends none. It never covers accepting a security risk: a security finding is fixed, not accepted. The controller records it on #1221, #1212 and #1216. #1216 carries bb7a73b67, so 1a's commit is taken into #1216 before it merges.

GATES: as the round's commission below, plus:
